BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UNCUT Presents: A 40th Anniversary Celebration of Charles Atlas’
  Hail The New Puritan  In partnership with Toronto Dance Theatre
DTSTART:20260605T193000
DTEND:20260605T193000
UID:c6f087eac08d49cd898ad81a73351465@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:To celebrate this trailblazing film\, the evening will include
 : 🕺”hey it was nice knowing you”\, a live dance performance by DOLL
 HEAD 2000 (aka Bray Cairns and Roberto Soria) 🎓 Introduction\, Framing 
 The Film by Amelia Ehrhardt from Weird Ballet 🎞️ Feature screening of
  Hail the New Puritan (dir. Charles Atlas\, UK\, 1986\, 85 min) Directed b
 y Charles Atlas and featuring the work of Scottish choreographer Michael C
 lark\, Hail The New Puritan is a fictionalized documentary capturing the r
 are intersection of ballet technique\, punk aesthetic\, and queer subcultu
 re that defined Clark’s groundbreaking work in the 1980s. With Leigh Bow
 ery in charge of Production Design and The Fall behind the soundtrack\, Ha
 il The New Puritan is more than a dance film\, it is a portrait of a radic
 al artistic moment that reshaped how contemporary dance could exist within
  popular and underground culture. Please note that the venue is non access
 ible due to a flight of stairs to access the theatre. The film will be pre
 sented in English\, with English subtitles. ‍
LOCATION:Winchester Street Theatre\, 80 Winchester St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/uncut-presents-a-40th-anniversary-celebrat
 ion-of-charles-atlas-hail-the-new-puritan-in-partnership-with-toronto-danc
 e-theatre
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
