DTSTART:20260607T203000
DTEND:20260607T203000
UID:9490fa8b670b53cf1c41b546b50a78b0@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Toronto&#x27\;s top queer and allied comedians take the stage 
 to raise funds for people living with HIV / AIDs! Toronto! Come out for a 
 hilarious night of queer comedy raising money for a great cause! This show
  features Toronto&#x27\;s top 2SLGBTQIA+ comics taking the stage to raise 
 funds for Friends for Life bike rally\, supporting people living with HIV/
 AIDs. Doors at 8 pm\, show from 8:30 - 10 pm. Right in the heart of the Vi
 llage at Pegasus on Church! All welcome\, including allies! How much are t
 ickets? Admission is free with donations gratefully accepted for the Frien
 ds for Life bike rally to support people living with HIV/AIDS. Donate here
  on Eventbrite or with cash in person at the event. Will it be weird if I 
 come solo? Nope! Feel free to pop in\, watch some comedy\, and dip after i
 f you aren&#x27\;t feeling social. If you&#x27\;re looking to mingle and m
 aybe have a meet cute\, feel free to introduce yourself to other audience 
 members and / or some of the comedians - everyone is really really nice. T
 his is all about community and supporting queer artists! Questions? Want t
 o come out but are a lil nervous? Totally feel free to reach out to us on 
 Instagram at @friendsofroxycomedy - its all about community! See you there
 ? 🤠🌈 --- The venue: The show takes place in the main area of Pegasus
  - head up the stairs and grab a seat in the front area with the stage The
  performance space and washrooms are up a flight of stairs. Once inside\, 
 there is no grade change. Unfortunately there is no lift or elevator All w
 ashrooms are gender inclusive Seating is self-assigned Community: All are 
 welcome at this event\, including allies\, that recognize this is a queer 
 space where we are inclusive and respectful of one another\, and where opp
 ressive behaviour won&#x27\;t fly At this show we don&#x27\;t punch down\,
  and isms\, phobias\, and aggressive crowd work will never be tolerated. T
 he show is hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbinary comedian who takes t
 his seriously AF\, and all the comedians agree to guidelines to keep the v
 ibes cute and inclusive This show will be fun filled and full of friendly 
 queers\, and the audience and comedian can make new friends and mix and mi
 ngle afterwards. If you are flying solo\, are nervous\, or have any questi
 ons\, feel free to DM the host @annasebastiencomedy on Instagram. This is 
 all about community! We all want a sexy\, healthy time! You are totally we
 lcome to wear a mask. If you are feeling sick\, please stay home! We&#x27\
 ;d be stoked if you rapid tested before the show. ‍
LOCATION:Pegasus\, 489B Church St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/friends-of-roxy---a-queer-comedy-fundraise
 r-7
