  Culture Issue 02 Launch Celebrate the release of the second issue of my m
 agazine with an evening of dance\, art\, and community. This event brings 
 the themes of the issue to life through a beginner/intermediate-friendly b
 allet class\, a curated photo exhibition\, and an interactive installation
 . Whether you’re a dancer\, curious about ballet\, or simply looking for
  a creative queer-centered space\, this night is designed for you! No prio
 r dance experience is needed. Your ticket includes event access\, a copy o
 f the new issue\, refreshments\, and the opportunity to connect with other
 s through art and shared experience. Limited capacity. 6:00 PM — Doors O
 pen Guests arrive\, check in\, explore the photo exhibition\, warm up for 
 class. (Please arrive on time if attending the ballet class. Comfortable c
 lothing is encouraged.) 6:15 PM — Ballet Class Begins A 90-minute beginn
 er/intermediate-friendly ballet class in the main studio. Taught by Nicole
  Prefontaine. 7:45 PM — Class Ends / Open Exhibition Continues Guests ar
 e invited to continue exploring the exhibition spaces\, connect with other
 s\, and enjoy refreshments. 8:30 PM — Event Concludes Final gallery view
 ing and closing conversations. ‍
