BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:By the Bi - An All Bi and Pan Comedy Show!
DTSTART:20260613T200000
DTEND:20260613T200000
UID:f11b32a16b331d11faecd9cfa2a029d5@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A Prideful night of comedy featuring EXCLUSIVELY bisexual and 
 pansexual comics! Bi-erasure this Pride? Not on our watch! Come celebrate 
 the B in 2SLGBTQIA+ with a vibie\, inclusive night of live comedy brought 
 to you by bi and pansexual comics! This is the perfect first stop on your 
 big turn-up Saturday night out OR an amazing way to celebrate Pride and be
  home in bed by 10 30 . Either way\, come through with your pals\, paramor
 e\, or polycule\, have a blast\, and leave feeling awesome for supporting 
 queer\, indie comedy. Featuring the hilarious: Sashka DC (@sashkadc\, she/
 they\, Just for Laughs Originals\, Toxic Comedy) James O&#x27\;Hara (@jame
 soharaaf\, he/him\, Winnipeg Comedy Festival\, Gender Venn Diagram Comedy)
  Isabel Zaw-Tun (@isabelzawtun\, she/her\, JFL\, Winnipeg Comedy Festival\
 , Debaters\, Crap Ass Comedy) Dre Pavez (@dre.pavez\, she/her\, Let&#x27\;
 s Go Comedy) Tracy Hamilton (@hamil.trace\, she/her\, Debaters\, CBC Laugh
  Out Loud\, Winnipeg Comedy Festival) Hosted and produced by Anna Sebastie
 n (@annasebastiencomedy\, they/them\, Just for Laughs Toronto\, Tea4Tea Al
 l Trans and Nonbinary Comedy\, Fresh Hot Babes). Tickets are $20 (we love 
 to pay queer artists for their labour!) but all welcome regardless of mean
 s - DM @annsebastiencomedy on Instagram for community / Pay What You Can p
 ricing. All welcome\, including allies\, and especially straight boyfriend
 s of bi women (we see you!). Grab your 3 or 4 lil bisexual beverages and c
 ome on laugh your butt off while supporting bi visibility this Pride! ----
 - The venue: The show takes place in the theatre space in the downstairs a
 rea of Tallboys. Take a left when you walk in and head downstairs! The ven
 ue unfortunately has a few barriers to access. There is a large step to en
 ter the main bar area. The theatre space and washrooms are located down a 
 staircase\, with tight corners from the bottom landing to the theatre. The
 re is also a single step from the basement hallway into the venue room. On
 ce inside\, there is no grade change. There is a communal gender neutral w
 ashroom with urinals and toilets\, a singe stall unmarked gender neutral w
 ashroom with a toilet\, and a woman&#x27\;s washroom with toilets. Seating
  is self-assigned and the venue is intimate\, so we recommend groups arriv
 e early so they can grab seats together Community: All are welcome at this
  event\, including allies\, that recognize this is a queer space where we 
 are inclusive and respectful of one another\, and where oppressive behavio
 ur won&#x27\;t fly At this show we only speak to our own identities\, we d
 on&#x27\;t punch down\, and isms\, phobias\, and aggressive crowd work wil
 l never be tolerated. The show is hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbina
 ry comedian who takes this seriously AF\, and all the comedians agree to c
 ommunity guidelines to keep the vibes as comfy as possible This show will 
 be fun filled and full of friendly queers\, and the audience and comedians
  can make new friends and mix and mingle afterwards. If you are flying sol
 o\, are nervous\, or have any questions\, feel free to DM the host @annase
 bastiencomedy on Instagram. This is all about community! We all want a sex
 y\, healthy Pride! If you are feeling sick\, please stay home! Refund requ
 ests will be honoured up to 24 hours before the show. You are totally welc
 ome to wear a mask\, and we&#x27\;d be stoked if you rapid tested before t
 he show. ‍
LOCATION:Tallboys Craft Beer House\, 838 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/by-the-bi---an-all-bi-and-pan-comedy-show
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
