BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queen Out Comedy - A Queer &amp\; Fem Open Mic!
DTSTART:20260614T183000
DTEND:20260614T183000
UID:c13fcdf4720417e60d7e5c8715616aa8@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A night of inclusive and vibie open mic comedy for the girls\,
  gays\, and theys! Looking for stage time to try out your silly lil jokes?
  Want to hang with other fem and / or queer comedians? Just want to cure y
 our Sunday scaries with some comedy? WELL you are in luck! Join us for Que
 en Out Open Mic Comedy! &lt\;33 The list goes out at 6:30pm\, with sign up
  on a first come\, first serve basis. The show starts promptly at 7 pm\, a
 nd will run to approximately 9 pm (depending on the number of sign ups). T
 his mic is open to anyone that identifies as a woman\, fem\, and / or memb
 er of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community. Sorry cis het dude comics - this one&#x27\
 ;s not for you. You are welcome to perform\, attend as an audience member 
 to support fem and queer comedy\, or both!! The fine print: 5 minute sets\
 , &quot\;warning light&quot\; at 4 minutes Free to attend with no purchase
  required\, BUT feel free to tip your host\, and please support the amazin
 g venue if you can. There are a range of nonalcoholic and alcoholic bevera
 ges for purchase as well as light food The venue is fully accessible for m
 obility aid users including communal and single stall gender neutral washr
 ooms at-grade All ages welcome but parental / guardian company is recommen
 ded for younger performers All are welcome to watch / support this event\,
  including cisgender heterosexual men\, but performance spaces are open on
 ly to fem and / or queer folx We will do our best to get everyone up who w
 ants to perform\, but we also need to be out of the venue before our allot
 ted time ends and want to keep the show length manageable and pleasant. Th
 is means we may have to cap or limit the list and / or reduce set times if
  we have more perfomers than expected. Please arrive as early as possible 
 to maximize your chances of getting on. Community guidelines are in place 
 for this show and will be discussed at the top. This includes no &quot\;pu
 nching down&quot\;\, no &quot\;isms&quot\; or phobias\, and no aggressive 
 crowd work. This mic is hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbinary comedia
 n who takes this seriously AF\, and who is committed to keeping the vibes 
 cute and inclusive. If content of a performance isn&#x27\;t aligned with t
 he guidelines\, the set will be ended early. We all want a sexy\, healthy 
 time! You are totally welcome to wear a mask. If you are feeling sick\, pl
 ease stay home! Questions? Want to come out but are a lil nervous? Totally
  feel free to reach out to the producer Anna Sebastien on Instagram at @an
 nasebastiencomedy - its all about community! ‍
LOCATION:Society Clubhouse\, 967 College Street
