UID:ed04ad6af16fb50fd4b19a45cbb6a1ac@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:☀️ Coast &amp\; Colour is back ☀️ The QTBIPOC Beach Da
 y returns to Hanlan’s Point for another summer of community and joy. Org
 anized by QTBIPOC community groups and collectives across Toronto\, Coast 
 &amp\; Colour is a space to gather\, unwind\, celebrate\, and spend the da
 y together by the water. Sapphic Shore will also be returning this year\, 
 creating space for sapphics to meet\, connect\, and build community by the
  beach 💖 We’ll be offering free ferry rides\, community-led activitie
 s\, music throughout the day\, and space to just exist and enjoy the beach
  together. The focus is on creating a welcoming and respectful environment
  for everyone sharing the space. Whether you’re coming to meet new peopl
 e\, reconnect with community\, dance a little\, or just spend the day in t
 he sun\, this day is for you. 📍 Hanlan’s Point Beach 📅 Saturday\, 
 July 4th\, 2026 ⏰ 11 am to sunset Follow @bipocsapphicshanlans for updat
 es\, ferry info\, partner announcements\, and more. Collaborating communit
 y groups: • Baila Sáfica @bailasaficatoronto • BIPOC Sapphics at Hanl
 an’s @bipocsapphicshanlans • Blackness Yes! @blocko_to • Bottoms Onl
 y! @bottomsonly_ • Las Malinches @lasmalinchesto • Lubun TO @lubun.to 
 • Marikass @marikass.collective • Meem Toronto @meemtoronto • The Qu
 eer Caribbean Network @queer.caribbean.network • ShikShook @shikshook.to
  • Untold Stories @blackuntoldstories • Wine Dung! @winedung.to ‍
LOCATION:Hanlan&#x27\;s Point Beach (near Sunset Trail 4 near the flagpole
 )\, Hanlan&#x27\;s
